From a8121dd54d3840672ef3a84944249b6e3d79c887 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Matuszewski <xanewok@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:19:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] tests : backend sampling under SPLIT_MODE_TENSOR

test-llama-archs --tp-sampling (ctest test-tp-backend-sampling) loads a
llama model with a 40960-token vocab on two CPU devices under tensor
split. It decodes ubatches without outputs, then 4 output rows, and
compares backend sampling with host sampling of the same TP logits (a twin
context without backend samplers): top-k candidates (ids and logits),
top-k + greedy, top-k + top-p + min-p + temp + dist, and the distribution
of top-k + temp + dist (4000 draws, total variation).

--tp-sampling-gpu runs the same on the first two GPUs. Only that covers a
lossy backend AllReduce: ids above 256 do not survive a BF16 exchange.
